{"id":"gravwell@0.0.1","nodes":{"1":{"id":1,"data":{"__meta":{"nickname":"Note","notes":"Rebuilds the Okta user-directory aggregates every hour from the newest record per user ($OKTA_LATEST_USERS) in the last 25 hours, which always includes the hosted ingester's daily full user snapshot. The queries run one after another; each returns metric,key,value rows; the template joins them into CSV lines and Ingest writes them to _aggs_okta_users stamped with the run time (ingesting the searches directly would stamp them with the start of the 25-hour window). The Okta User Overview and User Authentication Overview dashboards read only that tag; detections never do. Running the flow by hand ingests another copy; the dashboard uses the newest one.","inputs":[],"values":{}}},"inputs":{},"outputs":{},"position":[120,20],"name":"Annotation"},"2":{"id":2,"data":{"querystring":{"type":"Constant","value":"$OKTA_LATEST_USERS\n| json status as key\n| eval if (!has(key) || key == \"\" || key == \"null\") { key = \"(none)\"; }\n| stats count as value by key\n| eval metric = \"status\";\n| table metric key value"},"duration":{"type":"Constant","value":"PT25H"},"name":{"type":"Constant","value":"agg_status"},"__meta":{"nickname":null,"notes":null,"inputs":[],"values":{"querystring":{"type":{"kind":"string:query"},"value":"$OKTA_LATEST_USERS\n| json status as key\n| eval if (!has(key) || key == \"\" || key == \"null\") { key = \"(none)\"; }\n| stats count as value by key\n| eval metric = \"status\";\n| table metric key value"},"duration":{"type":{"kind":"string:isoduration","default":"PT1H"},"value":"PT25H"},"name":{"type":{"kind":"string","default":"search"},"value":"agg_status"}}}},"inputs":{"in":{"connections":[]}},"outputs":{"out":{"connections":[{"node":3,"input":"in","data":{}}]}},"position":[160,140],"name":"RunQuery"},"3":{"id":3,"data":{"search":{"type":"Variable","value":"agg_status"},"count":{"type":"Variable","value":"agg_status.Count"},"name":{"type":"Constant","value":"rows_s